            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-19057069"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://commbank.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=633bfc07a84c7f79c388ba81" class="user-hover" rel="633bfc07a84c7f79c388ba81" data-account-id="633bfc07a84c7f79c388ba81" accountid="633bfc07a84c7f79c388ba81" rel="noreferrer">Brent Mckendrick</a> this is a new requirement coming out of the approved policy which we are determining to be a MUST HAVE. Can you please confirm and if there is a delegate in your area whom we can work with please let us know. Thanks.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-19059925"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:f2ee1ef2-b992-4a99-8ef3-b300e1deeb05"
                id="word_commented_712020:f2ee1ef2-b992-4a99-8ef3-b300e1deeb05"
                href="https://commbank.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3Af2ee1ef2-b992-4a99-8ef3-b300e1deeb05">
                    A Muhammed Abdul Majeeth
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">13/Aug/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-19059925"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>Created an Issue Template and an actions workflow in <b><em>non prod</em></b> repo <a href="https://github.com/CBANPD-Self-Service-Portal/oss-audit-track/issues" title="smart-link" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/CBANPD-Self-Service-Portal/oss-audit-track/issues</a>  for testing this use case. The actions workflow is <em>yet to be</em> tested in non prod repo, since the non prod runners will not function after 10 P.M AEST Below explains the flow of Issue Template and actions workflow in detail:</p>

<p>Once an engineer submits the <b>OSS Contribution Request</b> issue after entering the details like Name, GHEC Handle, Line Manager Handle and so on, an automated approval chain is triggered. The workflow will post a comment on the issue showing all 5 required approvals and their current status. No need of manually tagging the person for approval, instead the actions workflow will automatically tag the person and ask for approval in the below mentioned sequential order.</p>

<ul>
	<li>&lt;&gt; Engineer submits form<br/>
        ↓<br/>
Line Manager is tagged automatically → posts "Approving this request"<br/>
        ↓<br/>
Chief / Principal Engineer is tagged automatically → posts "Approving this request"<br/>
        ↓<br/>
Open Source Reviewers team is tagged automatically → any one member posts "Approving this request"<br/>
        ↓<br/>
Engineering Practice team is tagged automatically → any one member posts "Approving this request"<br/>
        ↓<br/>
Group Strategy is tagged automatically → posts "Approving this request"<br/>
        ↓<br/>
Request fully approved ✅</li>
</ul>


<p>Each approval automatically notifies the next person in line and at all stages the workflow will show who are all the overall approvers and the next in line approver.</p>

<p>After each approval, the workflow then automatically updates the status table on the issue, confirms who approved, and calls out the next approver with clear instructions. If the wrong person tries to approve at any stage, they are told who the current approver should be and the chain does not advance.</p>

<p>Once all 5 approvals are obtained, the issue is marked <tt>fully-approved</tt> and remains open permanently as an audit record and after carefully reviewing the fields and approvals, the Issue can be closed.</p>

<p><b>Next Step of Actions:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Workflow in non prod repo to be tested</li>
	<li>Once tested successfully, create a similar setup in prod repo.</li>
</ul>

        </td></tr>
